        "paragraph_id": "16916A2D",
        "text": "Transport formulations"
      },
      {
        "container_path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_master.docx",
        "member": "word/document.xml",
        "start_xml_ordinal": 29404,
        "body_paragraph_zero_based": 773,
        "direct_body_paragraph_zero_based": 705,
        "paragraph_id": "63A2FB3D",
        "text": "In the present version of XBeach, two sediment transport formulations are available. The formulae of the two formulations are presented in the following sections. For both methods the total equilibrium sediment concentration is calculated with (2.88). In this equation the minimum value of the equilibrium sediment concentration (for both bed load en suspended load) compared to the maximum allowed sediment concentration (keyword: cmax)."
      }
    ],
    "following_nonempty_paragraphs": [
      {
        "container_path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_master.docx",
        "member": "word/document.xml",
        "start_xml_ordinal": 29593,
        "body_paragraph_zero_based": 777,
        "direct_body_paragraph_zero_based": 709,
        "paragraph_id": "448A8C7D",
        "text": "The transport formulations implemented into XBeach distinguishes bed load and suspended load transport. It is possible to in- and exclude these transports components (keywords: bed & sus, with bed = 1 one will include bed load transport). There is also a possibility to compute the total bulk transport rather than bed and suspended load separately (keyword: bulk = 1). The bed load will be calculated if it is suspended transport. On top of that this switch will have impact on how the bed slope effect (see Section 2.7.6) will be calculated"
      },
      {
        "container_path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_master.docx",
        "member": "word/document.xml",
        "start_xml_ordinal": 29655,
        "body_paragraph_zero_based": 778,
        "direct_body_paragraph_zero_based": 710,
        "paragraph_id": "123C8316",
        "text": "Soulsby-Van Rijn"
      }
    ],
    "table_cell": null,
